librga (2.2.0+git20260725.26a50ef-0ubuntu1~rk1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Update to librga-fork 26a50ef.
  * im2d: extend the 10-bit byte-stride conversion to TILE. The previous
    release limited it to RASTER on the premise that the kernel's tile stride
    math scales vir_w itself. It does not: the BSP derives the tile stride
    from vir_w * pixel_width * 8 (develop-5.10 and develop-6.1 alike) with
    pixel_width 1 for every 10-bit format, where the * 8 is the
    lines-per-tile-block factor, not a pixel-depth scale. Tile rows are
    byte-literal exactly like raster, and rga_convert_addr() offsets the UV
    plane by a flat vir_w * vir_h with no rd_mode distinction.
  * FBC keeps the pixel convention and remains excluded: its payload stride
    applies the format's own bytes-per-pixel to vir_w, and its register
    stride is the format-independent header stride.
  * Must be installed alongside a kernel carrying the matching TILE plane
    offset fix; a mismatched pair is wrong by 20% on the 10-bit TILE path,
    the same coupling as the 0072 / c80eea7 raster pair.
  * build: define LINUX once for every cmake target. Configuring without
    CMAKE_BUILD_TARGET matched no branch, leaving RgaUtils.cpp's #ifdef
    LINUX path locals undeclared; the meson build used by debian/rules
    always defined it, so this never affected the PPA build.
  * build: check fread() results in the file-dump helpers instead of
    returning success after a short or failed read.
  * The upstream date advances to 20260725 because the snapshot commit is
    2026-07-25 UTC. This is also required for ordering: a same-date bump to
    a hash beginning with a digit sorts below the 20260724.b8def3e
    predecessor under dpkg version comparison.

 -- Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>  Sat, 25 Jul 2026 06:35:00 +0000

librga (2.2.0+git20260724.b8def3e-0ubuntu1~rk1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Update to librga-fork b8def3e.
  * im2d: submit RASTER 10-bit vir_w as a byte stride to match the kernel
    RGA_BLIT ABI (compact x10/8, incompact x2); pairs with the kernel
    RGA3 byte-stride fix. TILE/FBC keep the pixel convention.
  * Also fixes the 10-bit UV plane offset on the virtual-address path.

 -- Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>  Thu, 24 Jul 2026 06:30:00 -0700

